    "content": "The 152nd running of the Kentucky Derby is scheduled for Saturday, May 2, 2026, at Churchill Downs in Louisville, Kentucky. As the first leg of the Triple Crown, this premier event is known as the \"Run for the Roses\" and will cap off a full week of racing and festivities. 2026 Kentucky Derby Key Details Date: Saturday, May 2, 2026 Location: Churchill Downs, 700 Central Ave, Louisville, KY Post Time: Approximately 6:57 p.m. ET (12th race of the day) Gates Open: 9:00 a.m. ET TV Coverage: NBC & Peacock Derby Week Events (April 25 – May 2, 2026) Derby Week features daily racing and special events leading up to the main race: Opening Day: Saturday, April 25, 2026 – Features the post-position draws for the Oaks and Derby. Sunday Funday: Sunday, April 26, 2026 – Returns with racing and brunch options. Dawn at the Downs: Monday, April 27, 2026 – Watch contenders train with breakfast options. 502'sDay: Tuesday, April 28, 2026 – A celebration of Louisville culture and local vendors. Winsday: Wednesday, April 29, 2026 – A day focused on community and non-profit support. Thurby: Thursday, April 30, 2026 – A celebration of Kentucky culture and heritage. Kentucky Oaks: Friday, May 1, 2026 – The 152nd Kentucky Oaks, featuring the \"Pink Out\" and Survivor Parade. Early 2026 Contenders and Odds As of March 2026, the field of contenders is taking shape through various prep races, with Paladin (9-1), Nearly (10-1), and Canaletto (15-1) emerging as early favorites. Other notable prospects following early 2026 races include: Stark Contrast (5-2 fav in 2026 Jeff Ruby Steaks) Fulleffort (7-2 in Jeff Ruby Steaks) Renegade (16-1) Silent Tactic (19-1) Tickets and Packages Availability: Tickets are already available for purchase, with most sold as 2-day packages covering both the Oaks and Derby. Options: Options range from luxurious clubhouse dining, such as the new Club SI Hospitality (offering premium, climate-controlled spaces and curated menus), to general admission in the infield party area. Purchasing: Tickets can be bought directly via KentuckyDerby.com, Ticketmaster, or by calling the Churchill Downs ticket office at 502-636-4447. KentuckyDerby.com Tips for Attending Dress Code: Fashion is a significant part of the tradition, with trends favoring bright colors, and for women, large hats and fascinators. Infield Experience: The cheapest option, the infield, is known for its party atmosphere and offers no reserved seating. Hotel Packages: Travel packages that include lodging and transportation are available through companies like Sports Traveler and Bucket List Events. Sports Traveler Bucket List Events",
